cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Bhāradvāja Vimāna: The Axis of Convergence"
message: "If you use this software or the results in it, please cite the paper."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bhāradvāja
    given-names: Ram
    affiliation: "Indian Institute of Technology Madras"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-20
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bhardvaja/vimana"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22027073"
abstract: >-
  For every p, integer or not, an elementary map multiplies the number of
  correct digits by exactly p at every step. In the mūla-bheda coordinate
  mu = (x-y)/(x+y) the map is the monomial mu -> mu^p, the digit law
  D_n = p^n D_0 is an equality, and the exponents form a group, so the order
  of convergence becomes a coordinate rather than a property read off after a
  method is built. This repository is the companion code: the map, the laws
  as tests, and a script that regenerates every number printed in the paper.
keywords:
  - order of convergence
  - iterative methods
  - split-complex numbers
  - arithmetic-geometric mean
  - Chebyshev polynomials
  - modular equation
  - mūla-bheda
  - Brahmagupta
